s", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RmKLHLTAFBLf9qmrL5AkmU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-gateway"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NG4dLwDAJ4Rp1Tj1iYJ6jf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The service is `payments-api`. Its history shows v5.0.0 as the most recent healthy production release, and v5.1.0 is degraded. I'll roll back to v5.0.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CpvjiSE1DB67gn5573Cij7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "version": "v5.0.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback was denied by a human reviewer, who said the problem is in `payments-worker`, not `payments-api`. I'll check that service rather than act on the original guess.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016psV2zM3pX5MXJjnXcTsuk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WTvtcMHm5WDFiMUhmy7akQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "`payments-worker` is unhealthy on v3.4.0 and was last healthy on v3.3.0, so I'll roll it back to v3.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XXNTMSs5Nwytkx59YZqfDa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VdTZhh1EuW3TDcpcP1CGiM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "Payments errors after deploy: payments-worker v3.4.0 rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "Payments errors began after this morning's deploy. payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in production (error rate 0.18) across us-east, us-west, and eu-west. Rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; rollback verified in all three regions. Note: an initial rollback attempt targeted payments-api (v5.1.0, also degraded at 0.18 error rate). It was denied by a human reviewer as the wrong service and was not executed. payments-api remains on v5.1.0 and needs separate investigation.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** The first rollback I tried targeted `payments-api`, which I had found by guessing service names. A human reviewer denied it as the wrong service and said the problem is in `payments-worker`. I did not retry it. `payments-worker` v3.4.0 was unhealthy in production with a 0.18 error rate. I rolled it back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy, and the rollout is verified in us-east, us-west, and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) is open against `payments-worker`. Its summary records the denied `payments-api` attempt.\n\n`payments-api` is still on v5.1.0, which is degraded with a 0.18 error rate, and it has not been rolled back. Its last healthy release was v5.0.0. Please confirm whether it is also affected before anyone rolls it back, since the reviewer ruled it out for this incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}